MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

This seems to be a problem of ggstance, see https://github.com/GuangchuangYu/ggtree/issues/96.

If you set the ylim manually, it works:
facet_plot(g.left, panel="Boxplot", data=melt_simple, geom_boxploth, mapping = aes(x=Abundance,group=label), outlier.shape=NA) + ylim(0, 135)

It is not informative, as you can check the distribution of abundance that contains outliers.
> hist(melt_simple$Abundance, plot=F)
$breaks
 [1]      0  50000 100000 150000 200000 250000 300000 350000 400000 450000
[11] 500000

$counts
 [1] 1152   11    3    6    2    2    2    0    0    1

$density
 [1] 1.954198e-05 1.865988e-07 5.089059e-08 1.017812e-07 3.392706e-08
 [6] 3.392706e-08 3.392706e-08 0.000000e+00 0.000000e+00 1.696353e-08

$mids
 [1]  25000  75000 125000 175000 225000 275000 325000 375000 425000 475000

$xname
[1] "melt_simple$Abundance"

$equidist
[1] TRUE

attr(,"class")
[1] "histogram"

If I restricted the Abundance to [0, 300], it works fine:
melt_simple = melt_simple[melt_simple$Abundance < 300,]
​facet_plot(g.left, panel="Boxplot", data=melt_simple, geom_boxploth, mapping = aes(x=Abundance,group=label), outlier.shape=NA) + ylim(0, 135)

​
​

